WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:27.680
14 criminal counts now name kalshi's founders in Utah's gambling fight. This is Prediction Markets Daily, Episode 37. Journalism and education never abet. After the charges, new briefs on Kalshi's federal appeal, an NFL rule that pushed a player out of a stake, a Rutgers survey on teen gambling, and a commission roundtable on around the clock trading, then the board and why a far off contract can trade below the chance a trader assigns it.

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:32.720
A day after the commodity futures trading commission asked a federal court to halt Utah's

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:37.540
enforcement, Attorney General Derek Brown filed criminal charges in Utah against the

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:41.580
company and co-founders, Terrick Mansour, and Luana Lopes-Lara.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:47.680
On top of the civil case already underway, the October 28 filing splits into one second

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:53.440
degree felony for a pattern of unlawful activity, 12 third degree felonies for online gambling

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:59.020
promotion, and one class A misdemeanor for general gambling promotion. In Utah, that

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:05.060
second-degree count can mean up to 15 years in prison and a $10,000 fine. A third-degree

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:11.760
felony can mean up to five years and $5,000. A class A misdemeanor can mean up to 364 days

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:18.280
and a $2,500 fine. Special agent Scott Egerman of the Attorney General's Office opened a

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:22.800
Kalshi account on September 13th with a Utah address and a debit card.

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:27.520
The platform asked him to confirm his location, and he confirmed he was in Utah.

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:35.620
He placed 12 sports wagers totaling $114.87 and booked a net loss of $25.10.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:39.760
Kalshi collected a fee of $3.78 on each trade.

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:42.860
The state issued summonses, not arrest warrants.

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:47.640
Mansour and Lopes Lara are to answer in third district court in Salt Lake County.

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:52.800
Brown said gambling is illegal in Utah, whether you place the bet, run the game, or promote

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:53.080
it.

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:58.240
He said calling it a prediction market does not change what it is, and federal registration

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:00.080
does not put a company above the law.

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:03.980
A call she spokesperson called the charge as a crazy overreach.

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:09.190
The company said it looks forward to stopping this in court, just as it did in Arizona, where

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:13.770
For U.S. District Judge Michael Liberty put a state criminal case on hold in April at

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:16.470
the request of the CFTC and the Justice Department.

00:02:17.438 --> 00:02:22.478
Thirty-seven states, plus Washington, D.C., and the Northern Mariana Islands, filed new

00:02:22.478 --> 00:02:27.178
Amicus Briefs Wednesday on Calche's appeal in the U.S. Court of Appeals for the 10th Circuit,

00:02:27.798 --> 00:02:33.438
gambling insider reports alongside the American Gaming Association, better markets, and tribal

00:02:33.438 --> 00:02:34.498
gaming organizations.

00:02:34.498 --> 00:02:40.138
Utah is the second state after Arizona to seek criminal penalties against the exchange.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:46.220
Sequan Barkley told Front Office Sports he used to hold equity in Polly Market and sold

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:51.060
it after the league made clear players cannot invest in or promote prediction market operators.

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:55.440
He said he is not in that right now and he is not allowed to be in that.

00:02:55.920 --> 00:03:01.460
He said the NFL briefs players before each season on investments and endorsements that prediction

00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:06.160
markets were on this year's list, and that he kind of had to get out of it. His shorter

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:11.880
version, he was in it before, but no bueno. The NFL confirmed Wednesday that it's bar on

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:17.320
investing in or promoting sports books also covers prediction markets, and it declined to discuss

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:23.760
his situation. Pauli Market declined to comment. The league told players in August 2025 that it would

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:29.420
treat these markets the same as sports betting. In January, an NFL Players Association spokesperson

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:33.400
said players cannot endorse companies such as Kalshi or Polymarket.

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:37.840
Draft Kings, Fandall, and Fanatics are the league's sportsbook partners.

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:40.700
Prediction markets stay out of its commercial deals.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:45.940
Their ads are barred, including during the Super Bowl, and the league says it prefers sports

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:47.680
wagering regulated by the states.

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:53.260
Earlier this month, the NFL asked the US Supreme Court to take up a New Jersey case on whether

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:57.360
federal commodities rules or state gambling laws govern these contracts.

00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:02.420
The NHL, Major League Baseball, and MLS have partnerships with Polymarket.

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:05.560
The NBA has deals with Polymarket and Calche.

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:11.000
NBA players are not barred from owning a stake, but they may not promote contracts tied

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:12.080
to NBA events.

00:04:13.145 --> 00:04:18.705
Rutgers University surveyed 1,677 Americans ages 13 to 27.

00:04:19.145 --> 00:04:26.565
52.5% had gambled in the previous year, including 42.7% of those ages 13 to 17.

00:04:26.565 --> 00:04:31.745
about 11% of the teenage gamblers were classed as high risk for problem gambling.

00:04:32.245 --> 00:04:39.305
18.9% of adolescents 13-17 gambled at least weekly. In the full 13-27 group,

00:04:39.665 --> 00:04:46.845
20.7% had bet on sports, 18.4% played season-long fantasy, 14% traded

00:04:46.845 --> 00:04:53.025
cryptocurrency, and 12.9% did high-risk stock trading. Social casino gaming was

00:04:53.025 --> 00:05:01.765
8.5% eSports betting 8.3% and prediction markets 6.6%. About 40% of the prediction market

00:05:01.765 --> 00:05:08.205
participants and 41% of social casino players were classed as high risk. Among high risk

00:05:08.205 --> 00:05:15.545
teenage gamblers 75.5% reported a family member who gambled and 61.2% had gambled with

00:05:15.545 --> 00:05:20.770
a family member. The Commodity Futures Trading Commission will host an industry roundtable

00:05:20.770 --> 00:05:25.990
on December 15th at its Washington headquarters on whether derivatives markets can trade around

00:05:25.990 --> 00:05:31.230
the clock. It builds on a request for comment from earlier this summer. The public session will

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:36.670
be live streamed. The brief covers overnight trading, tokenization, infrastructure, and staffing,

00:05:37.110 --> 00:05:42.370
and whether firms are ready to run that way. Agenda, speakers, and registration come later,

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:48.830
and the public may nominate speakers. Chairman Michael Selig said the agency will not take a one-size-fits-all

00:05:48.830 --> 00:05:53.890
approach to 24-7 trading, and that the point is to hear industry views across different

00:05:53.890 --> 00:05:54.710
asset classes.

00:05:55.806 --> 00:05:59.866
On the board today, the question of who will control the House is priced at an implied

00:05:59.866 --> 00:06:03.646
probability of 91% for the Democratic Party on CalShi.

00:06:04.306 --> 00:06:09.966
Polymarket price is the same party's House win in 2026 at 92.5%.

00:06:10.586 --> 00:06:16.306
CalShi's Senate contract price is Democratic control at 67%, up 4 points from the previous

00:06:16.306 --> 00:06:16.926
days price.

00:06:16.926 --> 00:06:24.466
Polymarket price is a democratic sweep of the 2026 midterms at 66.5%. A polymarket

00:06:24.466 --> 00:06:31.306
contract on a U.S. Iran ceasefire holding through October 31st is priced at 96.7%.

00:06:31.306 --> 00:06:38.086
The November 30th contract is at 39.5%, up three points in a day. Whether these venues

00:06:38.086 --> 00:06:43.206
are available and for which contracts depends on where you live, the rules differ by country,

00:06:43.206 --> 00:06:49.089
province and state, and they are changing. A contract that pays only if an event happens

00:06:49.089 --> 00:06:53.849
is a claim on cash that shows up when the contract settles. If that date is a year

00:06:53.849 --> 00:06:57.409
away, the payout is a year away even for someone who is already sure.

00:06:58.229 --> 00:07:03.449
Collateral posted to hold the position sits until then. Cash that is locked cannot be spent,

00:07:03.789 --> 00:07:08.329
lent, or posted somewhere else. Whatever that cash could have earned over the wait is a

00:07:08.329 --> 00:07:13.289
cost of holding the contract. A trader who must borrow the collateral or who has another

00:07:13.289 --> 00:07:17.909
use for it will not hand over today the full amount they think the contract is likely

00:07:17.909 --> 00:07:18.669
to pay later.

00:07:19.269 --> 00:07:22.749
The price can sit below the probability that trader actually holds.

00:07:23.309 --> 00:07:26.369
The gap is a charge for time, not a quieter forecast.

00:07:27.069 --> 00:07:31.789
Take a trader whose own belief is that the event is more likely than not, and a contract

00:07:31.789 --> 00:07:33.569
that cannot pay until next year.

00:07:34.129 --> 00:07:38.669
The most they will post today is that belief, reduced by what they give up while the collateral

00:07:38.669 --> 00:07:39.189
is stuck.

00:07:39.189 --> 00:07:43.989
track. The reduction tracks the return available on that cash over the life of the contract,

00:07:44.509 --> 00:07:49.269
plus any fee the venue takes for keeping the position open. A contract that settles

00:07:49.269 --> 00:07:54.229
next week has almost none of that weight. The same belief on the same event can therefore

00:07:54.229 --> 00:07:59.349
show a higher price on the near contract than on the far one. Reading the far price as

00:07:59.349 --> 00:08:04.769
if it were the near price treats two different claims as one forecast. Venues that pay interest

00:08:04.769 --> 00:08:09.809
on collateral change the arithmetic. If the cash posted earns a return while it waits,

00:08:10.309 --> 00:08:14.949
the trader is no longer giving up the whole alternative yield. The time-charge shrinks,

00:08:15.189 --> 00:08:20.749
and the price can sit closer to the probability the trader holds. A venue that pays nothing on margin

00:08:20.749 --> 00:08:26.009
leaves the full cost of the weight inside the price. Comparing a long-dated price on a venue

00:08:26.009 --> 00:08:31.569
that pays interest with one on a venue that does not, without knowing which is which, mixes a

00:08:31.569 --> 00:08:36.869
funding term into what looks like a probability. The adjustment fails when capital is not what

00:08:36.869 --> 00:08:42.369
binds. A position limit, a fee that does not scale with time, or a resolution rule that

00:08:42.369 --> 00:08:46.869
can void or rewrite the contract, can move the price for reasons that have nothing to do with

00:08:46.869 --> 00:08:52.509
the calendar. A thin market can print a number that no one was willing to defend with size. Play

00:08:52.509 --> 00:08:57.689
money, where the stake is reputation rather than cash that could have earned a return, does not

00:08:57.689 --> 00:09:02.849
carry the same time charge. Its long-dated price is not the same object as a cash price

00:09:02.849 --> 00:09:07.429
on a distant contract. So, read a far-dated price with the settlement date in view,

00:09:07.929 --> 00:09:13.489
and ask whether the collateral earns anything while it sits. A price below a stated belief is not by

00:09:13.489 --> 00:09:18.549
itself, a claim that the event is less likely. It may be the cost of waiting to be paid.

